(6482852, 962523, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TheDruid:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave this  five, not even rule of thirds. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Definitely disagree. Horizon is on a proper third, as it should be for a seascape. The initial posts are on intersecting thirds. There is a second horizon in the sky on another third. Beautiful ocean tones presented in thirds...a pair of triangles created by the horizon and posts ( right and left frame), and a center triangle created by the vanishing posts. Forget all of those thirds, check out the birds.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-07-27 21:52:37.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by TheDruid: I gave this  five, not even rule of thirds.   Definitely disagree. Horizon is on a proper third, as it should be for a seascape. The initial posts are on intersecting thirds. There is a second horizon in the sky on another third. Beautiful ocean tones presented in thirds...a pair of triangles created by the horizon and posts ( right and left frame), and a center triangle created by the vanishing posts. Forget all of those thirds, check out the birds.', '2011-07-27 22:51:57.000000', '2011-07-27 22:52:37.000000', 0),
